# billing

Billing.

A gRPC service with a REST mapping (grpc-gateway), built on
[kitchen](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/dungnh3/kitchen): `server` (gRPC +
REST + probes + graceful shutdown), `errs` and `i18n` (one error model for
gRPC and HTTP), `auth` (JWT/JWKS), `ratelimit`, `log` and `otelx`, with
PostgreSQL through `pg` (pgx) and sqlc, and goose migrations through `migrate`.

## Run

```bash
make up           # local dependencies in Docker (compose.yaml)
make run          # gRPC on :10000, REST on :8080, auth disabled
make run-worker   # the worker, in another terminal
make test         # unit tests and an integration test of the whole service
make lint
```

Try it:

```bash
curl -s localhost:8080/v1/items -d '{"title":"first"}'
curl -s localhost:8080/v1/items
```

## Layout

| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `proto/billing/v1/` | The API: messages, validation rules (protovalidate) and REST mapping |
| `gen/` | Generated by `make generate` from `proto/` (committed); OpenAPI in `gen/openapi/` |
| `cmd/server/` | `main`: logging, configuration, the commands (`serve | worker | migrate up|down|status`) |
| `internal/app/` | Wiring: telemetry, database, Redis, broker, auth, rate limits, server, worker; integration test |
| `internal/config/` | Configuration from environment variables |
| `internal/service/` | The API implementation, one file per domain (`item_service.go`) |
| `internal/store/` | Per domain: the types and store interface (`store.Items`) and their implementations (`memstore`, `pgstore`) |
| `internal/events/` | The events the service publishes (`ItemCreated`) |
| `internal/consumer/` | The event handlers of the worker |
| `internal/job/` | Periodic jobs, each on one worker replica at a time (lease on Redis) |
| `docs/ENV.md` | Environment variables |
| `.zen.yaml` | How zen generated the project; `make check` compares the managed files with it |
| `internal/store/pgstore/queries/` | SQL queries, one file per domain; `make generate` turns them into `sqlcdb` (committed) |
| `migrations/` | goose migrations, embedded in the binary |

## Change the API

A new resource with its CRUD API, store, queries and migration:

```bash
go run github.com/dungnh3/kitchen/zen@v0.1.0 add domain order
```

To change an existing API:

1. Edit `proto/billing/v1/*.proto` (validation rules go in the proto file).
2. Add a migration in `migrations/` and queries in `internal/store/pgstore/queries/`.
3. Run `make generate`, then implement the new methods in `internal/service`.

Return `errs` errors from methods (`errs.ErrNotFound`, `errs.BadRequest(...)`,
`errs.New(codes.FailedPrecondition, "REASON", ...)`); they become the same
`google.rpc.Status` on gRPC and the AIP-193 JSON error on REST, localized from
`Accept-Language`. Any other error is logged and the client sees a generic
internal error.

## Configuration

Every environment variable, its default and what production needs are in
[docs/ENV.md](docs/ENV.md).

Authentication is fail-closed: without `AUTH_*` (or an explicit
`AUTH_DISABLED=true` outside production) the service does not start, and an
unreachable JWKS stops startup too. Only the gRPC health service is public.
Restrict methods by scope with `auth.RequireScopes` in `internal/app`.

Every package logs through `github.com/dungnh3/kitchen/log` (`main` calls
`log.Setup`), and `.golangci.yml` keeps it that way: it denies `log/slog` and
the libraries behind every canonical kitchen package (raw Redis, SQL and HTTP
clients, `http.Server`, `status.New`, OTel SDK setup, ...). Use `redisx`,
`httpx`, `cache`, `lease`, `pubsub`, `timex` and friends instead.

Rate limits are shared by every instance through Redis
(`github.com/dungnh3/kitchen/ratelimit/redis`).

## Migrations

```bash
server migrate up        # apply pending migrations (run as a deploy step / init container)
server migrate down      # roll back the last one
server migrate status
```

A Postgres advisory lock serializes concurrent runs. `DB_MIGRATE_ON_START=true`
runs `up` at startup instead, which suits local development.

## Worker

`server worker` does the background work; deploy it as its own Deployment
from the same image (`/server worker`). It stops gracefully on SIGTERM.

- **Events.** `pgstore.CreateItem` writes the item and its `ItemCreated`
  event in one transaction (transactional outbox,
  `github.com/dungnh3/kitchen/pubsub/outbox/pgx`); the worker relays the
  outbox to the broker, so an event is enqueued if and only if its item is
  stored, and the relay publishes it at least once.
- **Consumers.** `internal/consumer` handles the events with
  `github.com/dungnh3/kitchen/pubsub`. Delivery is at least once, so
  handlers must be idempotent. Return `nil` to ack, an error to retry, and
  `pubsub.Permanent(err)` to dead-letter. `zen add consumer <name>`
  adds a consumer with its subscription settings.
- **Jobs.** `internal/job` runs each job on one replica at a time under a
  Redis lease. `zen add job <name> -every 5m` adds one; a run must stop
  when its context is cancelled.
- **Probes.** Set `ADMIN_ADDR` and point the worker's probes at `/livez` and
  `/readyz` on it.

## Markers

`zen add` inserts code before marker comments such as
`// zen:services`; keep them where they are.

## Managed files

`.golangci.yml`, `Dockerfile`, `.dockerignore`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
and `buf.gen.yaml` are managed by zen: CI and `make check` fail when one
of them is edited by hand, and `make check ARGS=-write` updates them to the
current template. To own one of them, remove it from `managed` in
`.zen.yaml`.

## Deploy

`make docker` builds a static binary into a distroless image that runs as
nonroot. For private modules, pass `--build-arg GOPRIVATE=...` and
`--secret id=netrc,src=$HOME/.netrc`; the credentials never land in a layer.
Point the Kubernetes probes at `/livez` and `/readyz` on the HTTP port (or the
admin port).
